# ANTUMBRA code ownership and rail routing.
#
# The consensus surface — every crate, every archived vector set,
# every architecture decision record — is rail C: changes travel
# through a pull request carrying the `rail-c` label, with an ADR
# in the diff whenever crate sources change, gated by the full CI
# wall. ci/merge_rails.py enforces the routing mechanically and
# branch protection requires every check; this file documents the
# review intent behind the predicate.
#
# Everything else (scripts, simulations, CI, docs tooling) is
# rail B: mergeable without the rail-C ceremony, and never allowed
# to touch code/crates.

